# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party material: vendor installers, extracted/decompiled vendor software
# and downloaded analysis tools.
#
# None of this is ours to redistribute, and it is ~3 GB. The research documents
# reference paths inside third-party/ so the evidence trail stays readable, but
# the files themselves must be fetched from the vendor to reproduce the work -
# third-party/README.md lists what belongs where.
#
# Ignoring the contents rather than the folder: with "third-party/" git would not
# descend into it at all and the README below could not be un-ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
third-party/*
!third-party/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine- and user-specific
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Runtime state written by the app during research runs; per-machine, not source.
research/state/

# Compiled artefacts kept next to the recovery record. They were the INPUT to the
# decompilation documented in research/DIAGNOSTICS-RECOVERY.md, not source - and both a
# .NET assembly and its PDB embed the absolute source path of the machine that built
# them, which is exactly the kind of detail that must not be published. The recovered and
# decompiled C# beside them is the part that carries the evidence, and that stays.
research/recovery/**/*.dll
research/recovery/**/*.pdb

# Log files, wherever they land. The app itself writes to %LocalAppData%, but a
# stray copy in the tree must never be committed - logs can contain paths.
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Offscreen render output: regenerated by AorusControl.UiChecks on every run, and large.
research/runs/ui/
research/runs/profile-ui/
